  "summary_en": "Brazil's consolidated NR-12 regulatory standard on occupational safety in machinery and equipment, with annexes for presses, injection moulding, agricultural machines, aerial lifts and others. It sets protective-guarding, interlock, emergency-stop, risk-assessment, training and manufacturer obligations, and deems robotic systems compliant if they follow ISO 10218 and ISO/TS 15066.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Employers must adopt collective, then administrative, then individual protective measures based on risk assessment.",
   "Robotic systems complying with ABNT ISO 10218-1/-2 and ISO/TS 15066 are deemed compliant (12.1.12).",
   "Safety systems, interlocks and emergency stops are mandatory, with safety categories under ISO 13849/NBR 14153.",
   "Manufacture, import, sale and leasing of non-compliant machines is prohibited.",
   "Mandatory worker training, manuals in Portuguese, and maintenance records."
  ],
